---
const faqs: [string, string][] = [
  [
    'How do I get an invite?',
    'Zephyr is opening a few seats at a time. Request an invite with your email and we’ll send a single-use link when a spot opens, or ask a Zephyr member: each member can invite a few people a month. Clients you share galleries with never need an account.',
  ],
  [
    'Is the free plan really free?',
    'Yes. You get 5 GB, unlimited Zephyr AI on your device, 30 cloud credits a month for background removal, and three passcode galleries. Ads appear inside the app on the free plan; they never appear on galleries you share or inside the editor.',
  ],
  [
    'What happens to my original photos?',
    'Nothing. Edits are saved as a small recipe next to each photo, so you can reset, tweak or copy them at any time and export a fresh file whenever you like.',
  ],
  [
    'How safe is a six-digit passcode?',
    'It is the second lock. The link itself is a long random token, the code is checked on our servers, and five wrong tries in 15 minutes pauses that visitor. You can set an expiry and revoke a link at any moment.',
  ],
  [
    'What is a Zephyr AI credit?',
    'Most Zephyr AI runs on your device and is free and unlimited on every plan: auto-enhance, HDR, colour match, cleanup and face grouping. Credits are only for studio background removal, which runs on a cloud GPU at 1 credit per photo. Unused monthly credits don’t roll over; top-up credits do.',
  ],
  [
    'Do I have to install anything?',
    'No. Zephyr runs in any modern browser. Installing it adds an icon, opens it full screen and makes it faster to start. On iPhone and iPad, open Zephyr in Safari, tap Share, then Add to Home Screen.',
  ],
  [
    'Can I cancel or downgrade any time?',
    'Yes, from Settings › Plan. Your photos stay put; if you’re over the free storage you can still view and download them, you just can’t upload more until you’re under.',
  ],
];
---
<section id="faq" class="section">
  <div class="wrap faq">
    <header class="section-head section-head--center">
      <span class="eyebrow">Questions</span>
      <h2 class="h2">Good to know</h2>
    </header>
    <div class="faq__list">
      {
        faqs.map(([q, a], i) => (
          <details open={i === 0}>
            <summary>
              {q}
              <span class="faq__plus" aria-hidden="true" />
            </summary>
            <p>{a}</p>
          </details>
        ))
      }
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
<style>
  .faq {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 32px;
  }
  .faq__list {
    max-width: 820px;
    width: 100%;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }
  details {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
    padding: 20px 4px;
  }
  details:last-child {
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  summary {
    cursor: pointer;
    list-style: none;
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 16px;
    font-size: 18px;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
  }
  summary::-webkit-details-marker {
    display: none;
  }
  .faq__plus {
    position: relative;
    width: 14px;
    height: 14px;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }
  .faq__plus::before,
  .faq__plus::after {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    top: 6px;
    width: 14px;
    height: 2px;
    border-radius: 2px;
    background: var(--muted);
    transition: transform 200ms var(--ease-out);
  }
  .faq__plus::after {
    transform: rotate(90deg);
  }
  details[open] .faq__plus::after {
    transform: rotate(0deg);
  }
  details p {
    margin-top: 12px;
    font-size: 15px;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--muted);
    max-width: 720px;
  }
</style>
